<%#
  Vendored from electron-installer-debian's resources/desktop.ejs (3.2.0), with one
  change: StartupNotify is false rather than true.

  Statusky has no window to raise, so the launch feedback the startup notification
  protocol asks for — a bouncing cursor, then a taskbar entry — never resolves into
  anything the user can see, and the desktop shell eventually gives up on its own after
  several seconds of pretending the app is starting. electron-builder expressed this as
  `linux.desktop.entry.StartupNotify`; @electron-forge/maker-deb has no per-key override
  of the desktop entry, only `desktopTemplate`, so the whole template comes along.

  That means owning it: if electron-installer-debian changes its template upstream, this
  copy silently keeps the old one. It is eleven lines, so the cost of re-reading it at
  upgrade time is small, but it is not zero.
-%>
[Desktop Entry]
<% if (productName) { %>Name=<%= productName %>
<% } %><% if (description) { %>Comment=<%= description %>
<% } %><% if (genericName) { %>GenericName=<%= genericName %>
<% } %><% if (name) { %>Exec=<%= name %> %U
Icon=<%= name %>
<% } %>Type=Application
StartupNotify=false
<% if (categories && categories.length) { %>Categories=<%= categories.join(';') %>;
<% } %><% if (mimeType && mimeType.length) { %>MimeType=<%= mimeType.join(';') %>;
<% } %>
